course: dictionary
lesson: 14803
title: The pupal stage
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some insects change their whole body shape as they grow. Scientists call this complete metamorphosis. It has four stages: egg, larva, pupa, adult. The word pupal means to do with a pupa, the resting stage between larva and adult.
explain: «The caterpillar spun a silk case and entered the pupal stage.» The clues are spun a silk case and entered. The caterpillar stopped moving about and rested inside a case, so pupal stage means the resting time when it changes shape.
explain: «Inside the pupal case, the larva slowly turned into an adult moth.» The word case tells you the pupa is protected. Try the swap check: put «resting» in place of pupal and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A pupa is the resting stage in an insect's life between larva and adult.
fact: Pupal is an adjective, so it describes a thing: «pupal stage», «pupal case», «pupal skin».
fact: A butterfly's pupa is called a chrysalis.
fact: Insects with complete metamorphosis, such as butterflies, moths, beetles and flies, all go through a pupal stage.
fact: Grasshoppers do not have a pupal stage: they hatch looking like small adults and grow bigger.
exercise: «The caterpillar spun a silk case and entered the pupal stage.» What does pupal mean? | * The resting stage when an insect changes shape inside a case | The egg stage, before anything hatches | The adult stage when wings are fully grown | The stage when an insect eats the most
exercise: «Inside the pupal case, the larva slowly turned into an adult moth.» Find and copy the word that tells you the case belongs to a pupa. | moth | slowly | * pupal | larva
exercise: In complete metamorphosis, where does the pupal stage come? | * After the larva, before the adult | Straight after the egg | After the adult has died | Before the egg
test: Mia says a butterfly's pupa is called a chrysalis. What is a chrysalis? | A small green leaf | A full-grown adult butterfly | A larva that is still hatching | * The pupa of a butterfly
test: Which of these insects goes through a pupal stage? | A grasshopper, which hatches looking like a small adult | * A housefly | A spider | A worm
exam: Which order is correct for complete metamorphosis? | egg, pupa, larva, adult | adult, egg, larva, pupa | larva, egg, adult, pupa | * egg, larva, pupa, adult
